WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.160
This magical tale about the power of storytelling
and faith has so many messages that, like

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.200
The NeverEnding Story itself, are timeless.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.360
Let's hop on Falkor and explore.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.480
This is the ending of The NeverEnding Story,
finally explained.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.940
The NeverEnding Story takes the tried and
true formula of the Hero's Journey and gives

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.859
it an interesting narrative twist by doubling
up on protagonists.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:29.700
Atreyu is tasked with finding a cure for the
Childlike Empress, whose deathly illness threatens

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:34.530
the fabric of Fantasia while a dark force
called the Nothing eats everything in its

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.020
path.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:40.580
From the Ivory Tower to the Swamps of Sadness,
the Southern Oracle, and the ends of Fantasia

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.000
itself, Atreyu searches for a cure at great
personal loss.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.420
He loses his horse and best friend Artax,
which threatens the courage and resolve that

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.160
got him on this journey in the first place.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:58.420
Fortunately, he makes a new friend in luck
dragon Falkor, who helps him get back on track.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:04.440
At the first gate of the Southern Oracle,
Atreyu faces another test: this time he must

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.660
confront his own sense of self-worth, proving
he believes in himself.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:14.620
He then has to confront the vision of his
true self in a mousy little boy named Bastian

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:17.160
who is reading a book far, far away.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.070
Part of Atreyu's journey is complete when
he learns the Childlike Empress needs a new

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:27.480
name, and only a human child can bestow it,
but there are more setbacks in store.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:33.240
Atreyu loses Falkor and his magical talisman,
and is forced to confront the Nothing's minion

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.440
with nothing but his own wits and strength.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.680
Meanwhile, Bastian has his own part to play
in The NeverEnding Story.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.520
At first, it seems like a simple framing sequence,
with Bastian reading a storybook about the

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.080
events unfolding for Atreyu and Fantasia.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:52.360
He's grieving the loss of a mother who seemed
to support her son's sensitivity and daydreaming,

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:55.060
and his escape into flights of fancy are his
coping method.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:01.060
When Atreyu loses Artax, Bastian weeps along
with him, because he has felt that loss himself.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:07.680
"My horse died, I nearly drowned, I barely
got away from the nothing!"

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:13.000
As he reads, Bastian realizes that he might
be the most important hero of them all.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.400
And to honor his cherished mother and her
memory, he even gives her name to the Childlike

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.880
Empress, saving her and Fantasia.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.750
"Moon Child."

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.519
If it seems silly that a new name might save
someone's life, then you haven't considered

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.440
the power of what we call things.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.790
Bastian is called terrible names by the school
bullies, which certainly affects how he feels

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:39.920
and sees himself.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:44.920
With the arrival of the Nothing, the Childlike
Empress also loses an aspect of herself that

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.140
must be reinvented.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:51.480
Her new name is a new start, not just for
the Empress, but for her whole world.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:56.420
As Bastian makes his wishes, he ensures that
all the friendships made before the Nothing's

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.200
rampage remained intact.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.799
He ultimately gets to experience a ride on
Falkor firsthand, and even gives his bullies

00:03:03.799 --> 00:03:05.629
a taste of their own terrible medicine.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:12.140
As the Nothing sweeps across Fantasia, a ragtag
bunch meets in the Howling Forest on their

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:17.569
way to the Ivory Tower: The Rock Biter, the
Night Hob and his Stupid Bat, as well as Teeny

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:19.180
Weeny and his Racing Snail.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:23.540
They are all members of different Fantasian
groups with the same mission of beseeching

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.280
the Childlike Empress for help restoring their
lands.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:31.340
This unlikely group quickly becomes friends
as they realize how each can help the others.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:35.760
The Night Hob is able to fly to the top of
the Ivory Tower and hear the news.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:40.749
The Rock Biter offers all the little ones
protection, and the Racing Snail is here to

00:03:40.749 --> 00:03:44.340
shatter preconceived notions of what certain
kinds of creatures can do.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:49.260
What bonds them is the shared loss of their
ancestral lands through the power of dark

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:54.419
forces, which brings a theme of colonization
into The NeverEnding Story's mix and leads

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.760
to a very grim moment when the Nothing snatches
the Rock Biter's friends right from under

00:03:58.760 --> 00:03:59.260
him.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:07.460
"They look like big, good, strong hands, don't
they?"

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:12.900
The Rock Biter gives up hope and allows the
Nothing to take him, but because of Bastian's

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:18.310
clever wishes, he and his comrades are eventually
reunited and continue their shared friendship

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.400
through the collective trauma they all survived.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:26.300
One of the most satisfying things about a
fairy tale like The NeverEnding Story is how

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.720
far into destruction we travel before the
world is restored to rights.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:36.060
The Nothing destroys all of Fantasia except
for a single grain of sand before Bastian

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.160
heals the Empress with her new name.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:43.380
The forces of darkness are defeated, but there
is still work to do to properly restore all

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.500
that's been damaged.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.950
Bastian has a huge job ahead of him now that
he's no longer just an armchair hero, and

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:55.710
when the Empress grants Bastian all the wishes
he needs to recreate Fantasia, it's a victory

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.840
against hopelessness.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:02.720
When we see Fantasia rebuilt in a new form
of glory it reminds us that maintaining hope

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:07.530
in even the bleakest of circumstances is a
life-affirming act — and one we should strive

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:09.380
to cultivate as Bastian does.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:14.400
Falkor might be the single most beloved character
in The NeverEnding Story.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:18.940
Between his hearty chuckle and his friendly
canine features, Falkor is a reminder that

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:22.820
we must always fight against the kind of hopelessness
embodied by the Nothing.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:28.440
While many times luck is actually a product
of good circumstances, timing, and privilege,

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:33.410
the luck symbolized by Falkor is about the
faith that goodness — and good people — will

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:34.420
ultimately prevail.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:39.260
Even when Atreyu is convinced that he failed
to find the human child who could give the

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:44.920
Empress a new name, Falkor comforts him and
reminds him that he did his very best, and

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.580
that kind reminder is what draws viewers to
the luck dragon.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:53.460
In a scene that has been traumatizing children
alike for decades, Atreyu loses his beloved

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.400
horse in the Swamps of Sadness.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.240
Even today, people who have seen The NeverEnding
Story a hundred times know it as the most

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:05.110
brutal scene in the film, and some will even
leave the room to avoid shedding tears.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:09.440
Looking at the big picture, though, the terrible
events in the Swamps of Sadness are a perfect

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:12.600
metaphor for grief, loss, and childhood trauma.

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:18.540
This is probably why adults still have a visceral
reaction to the incident even years later,

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:23.180
because we remember being Atreyu's age and
having to navigate our own losses in different

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:23.740
ways.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:28.860
What ends up being beautiful about this painful
scene is how it shows us that even a warrior

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.200
isn't immune to grief.

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:36.040
For Bastian, the moment allows him to feel
his own grief, and begin to process the trauma

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.080
of losing his mother, and teaches him one
of the movie's lessons.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:42.120
"It has to hurt if it's to heal."

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.720
Avoidance doesn't make wounds go away, and
pain has the power to remind us we are still

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:48.960
alive and healing.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:54.760
Sometimes, people become more cynical as they
get older, and this can quickly turn into

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.240
bitterness and resentment.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:01.270
It certainly does with Bastian's father, who
is all business and can't understand why his

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.900
son can't move on from his mother's death
as quickly.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:08.140
He sees Bastian's sensitivity as weakness,
and so does the Nothing.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:15.000
"Because people who have no hopes are easy
to control."

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:20.080
This is a scarily true statement in our own
human world, where every day, people lose

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.420
hope and turn to all kinds of ways not to
care about others.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:29.460
Morla the Ancient one embodies this despair,
constantly saying that nothing matters, echoing

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:32.600
the apathy and cynicism that we often see
in adults.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:38.020
Atreyu and Bastian, however, both refuse to
accept these supposedly grown-up truths.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:43.600
One of The NeverEnding Story's most important
messages is having faith in the competence

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:44.260
of children.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.280
Just because someone is young doesn't make
them incapable of great feats.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:53.940
"He simply can't imagine one little boy could
be that important."

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:58.990
Sadly, Bastian has been bullied for the traits
that make him the ideal child to help save

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:03.360
Fantasia, so he has no idea how much power
he holds in his heart and imagination.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:08.120
When he learns his own strength, though, it's
a lesson he'll hopefully never forget.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:15.000
The NeverEnding Story is packed full of important
themes and messages, but one of the most fundamental

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:19.280
is about the dangers of bullying, including
the way that parents treat their children.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:24.380
The bullying that Bastian deals with from
his classmates is awful and humiliating, but

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:28.990
the quiet bullying he endures from his father
is far more insidious than being tossed into

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:30.600
a dumpster by his classmates.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:36.060
He berates his son for his keen imagination
and the way he expresses himself in ways that

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:40.380
are all healthy coping mechanisms for a child
grieving the recent loss of his mother.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:45.300
This is one of the more painful aspects of
the film, and explains why Bastian wouldn't

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:49.360
want to come back to Earth so quickly once
he finally visits Fantasia.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:55.380
Many kids who are sensitive and imaginative
find sanctuary in books and stories on their

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.160
best days.

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:01.040
On a bad day, however, like the one that sees
Bastian bullied by both his father and the

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:06.040
regular trio of tormentors at school, a book
is an even more valuable tool of escape.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.470
He simply cannot deal with the real world,
and the only thing that makes sense to him

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.780
is digging into a book he's never read before.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:18.339
There's an almost religious kind of sanctuary
in the way the film presents the act of reading,

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.380
and there's more to it than just escapism.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:25.480
As the bookseller, Mr. Coreander, says, a
safe book allows you to return to yourself

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.100
unscathed by the end.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:32.579
But a dangerous book will change you, and
fundamentally change how you see and experience

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:33.080
the world.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:39.380
The NeverEnding Story also introduces young
audiences to the notion of metatextuality,

00:09:39.389 --> 00:09:40.819
stories within stories.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:47.080
"Just as he is sharing your adventures, others
are sharing his."

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:52.310
This narrative trick can draw readers and
viewers even deeper into a story by making

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:56.870
us a part of it, and that's a huge reason
why The NeverEnding Story still resonates

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.000
with audiences today.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:04.120
As a film, The NeverEnding Story focuses on
adapting on the first half of Michael Ende's

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:07.520
beautiful book, about how a little boy saves
the world through reading.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:13.329
The NeverEnding Story II: The Next Chapter
was released in 1990 with an entirely new

00:10:13.329 --> 00:10:17.400
cast except for grouchy bookstore owner Carl
Conrad Coreander.

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:22.180
In this sequel, Bastian is trying to get over
his fear of heights, which he does not have

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.200
when he's riding on the back of a luck dragon.

00:10:24.649 --> 00:10:30.240
When the Auryn, the mystical talisman carried
by Atreyu, calls to him, he returns to Fantasia

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.260
where a new evil, the Emptiness, is being
fueled by a sorceress.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:40.200
She tricks Bastian into making wishes, all
the while stealing his memories of Earth and

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:40.700
home.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:46.020
1994's The Neverending Story III diverges
completely from Ende's book and returns with

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:47.620
yet another new cast.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:53.460
This time Bastian battles the Nasty, played
by Jack Black in one of his first major roles,

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:56.259
and reunites with many characters from the
original film.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:02.480
When Atreyu reaches the boundaries of Fantasia,
he finds a temple in ruins with elaborate

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:02.980
paintings.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:07.280
He's shocked to see the paintings are of him
and everything he survived.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:12.790
The NeverEnding Story suggests that Atreyu's
journey, like the classic "Hero's Journey"

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:17.900
structure that it follows, has happened many
times before, and will probably happen again.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:24.100
This cycle of life and destruction and life
emerging again is, in fact, a neverending

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:28.720
story, but more than that, the fight against
apathy and hopelessness and replacing them

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.800
with hope and faith is a story without an
ending, too.

00:11:32.529 --> 00:11:37.060
Like the symbol of two snakes entwined eating
their own tails, these important themes from

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:39.560
the story continue to be relevant in the human
world.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:46.069
The fact that after so many decades people
still watch, engage with, and adore The NeverEnding

00:11:46.069 --> 00:11:50.140
Story is simply a testament to the everlasting
power of this triumphant tale.

